# GitHub Linguist overrides — controls what the repository's Languages panel
# counts. See https://github.com/github-linguist/linguist#using-gitattributes
#
# Linguist analyses the default branch on every push. These rules make that
# analysis stable and honest rather than leaving it to heuristics.

# Build output and the lockfile are generated. Neither is committed today, but
# excluding them means a future commit of dist/ cannot skew the panel toward
# "minified JavaScript".
dist/**           linguist-generated
package-lock.json linguist-generated

# The sandbox page is HTML carrying a large inline <script> and <style> block.
# Pin its classification so content heuristics cannot tip it toward JavaScript
# and erase the markup from the panel.
demo/index.html   linguist-language=HTML

# Tests, demo harness and build scripts are real source and are counted on
# purpose. They are TypeScript and JavaScript respectively, so they change the
# proportions in the panel but never which languages appear.
